WEBVTT

00:05.440 --> 00:07.640
Morlock-san, we should do that one.

00:07.960 --> 00:09.400
That one? Which is that?

00:09.400 --> 00:11.490
Hey, geezer, hurry up!

00:11.490 --> 00:13.160
Those ripples it gave rise to...

00:13.160 --> 00:16.240
Those ripples it gave rise 
to shall serve as guides.

00:16.680 --> 00:17.990
<i>Just one more passage!</i>

00:18.390 --> 00:20.910
Guide me and me alone...

00:20.910 --> 00:23.000
to a Moment of Solitude!

00:32.220 --> 00:33.030
Huh?

00:35.020 --> 00:36.780
Let's see...

00:36.780 --> 00:39.060
I feel like there's 
something I'm supposed to do.

00:39.060 --> 00:42.020
<b>Before time passes once more,</b>

00:39.060 --> 00:42.020
<b>counting to 100</b>

00:39.060 --> 00:42.020
<b>is possible</b>

00:42.310 --> 00:47.430
<i>That world I had always envisioned</i>

00:47.430 --> 00:51.080
<i>Could I have found it?</i>

00:59.950 --> 01:04.570
<i>I lived my days at someone 
else's convenience</i>

01:04.990 --> 01:09.200
<i>Gaining nothing but compromises and regrets</i>

01:09.200 --> 01:11.340
<i>Because I always felt that</i>

01:11.340 --> 01:15.230
<i>Even if it wasn't me standing here</i>

01:15.230 --> 01:19.270
<i>The world would still keep moving forward</i>

01:19.270 --> 01:23.070
<i>Even after I lost it</i>

01:23.070 --> 01:25.350
<i>And its colors faded</i>

01:25.350 --> 01:29.430
<i>The dream from that hazily remembered day</i>

01:29.430 --> 01:31.390
<i>Still remained</i>

01:31.390 --> 01:33.820
<i>The thing that only I can do</i>

01:33.820 --> 01:36.540
<i>And the scenery that I left behind</i>

01:36.540 --> 01:44.060
<i>I was just looking for an answer 
from some other time</i>

01:45.390 --> 01:50.250
<i>Those things that don't change</i>

01:50.250 --> 01:55.830
<i>And those words I protected so carefully</i>

01:55.830 --> 02:00.470
<i>Even if they're all just 
unattractive junk to others</i>

02:00.470 --> 02:08.870
<i>They're all treasures 
that I will never give up</i>

02:20.000 --> 02:21.640
Let's see...

02:22.290 --> 02:23.400
Huh?

02:40.390 --> 02:41.560
What?

02:42.430 --> 02:43.460
An enemy?

02:46.020 --> 02:48.460
Lafa's been paralyzed?

02:48.460 --> 02:50.600
No, she's flying, so that's not it.

02:51.290 --> 02:52.550
I don't understand.

02:53.910 --> 02:56.400
Saitou! What's going on?

02:57.000 --> 02:58.290
Saitou!

02:58.290 --> 02:59.360
Hey!

03:02.940 --> 03:03.860
Oh.

03:04.660 --> 03:08.370
"Attack the eyes with magic."

03:14.160 --> 03:16.020
<i>Now I remember.</i>

03:16.020 --> 03:18.130
<i>Back then, you...</i>

03:23.070 --> 03:25.190
Morlock-san, keep going.

03:25.640 --> 03:28.120
So that it wouldn't matter if I forgot,

03:28.120 --> 03:31.650
you used the magic pen you 
brought from your world to...

03:32.910 --> 03:35.100
I am such a...

03:35.760 --> 03:39.110
such a lucky fellow!

03:39.370 --> 03:40.360
Saitou!

03:40.360 --> 03:41.620
Lafanpan!

03:41.620 --> 03:42.860
Raelza!

03:44.900 --> 03:49.470
To this old fool, you, my son 
and daughters, are always exceptional!

03:50.120 --> 03:53.380
All of you, who would threaten my children...

03:53.380 --> 03:54.460
I will never forgive you!

03:54.460 --> 03:57.210
Earth, water, fire, and wind 
of the Four Spirit Sources...

03:57.610 --> 03:59.720
Void rank, first class, tier ten...

04:00.000 --> 04:04.140
Sorcery, in the name 
of Bergheim Crom, activate!

04:06.050 --> 04:09.130
This secret art raises magical 
power to its utmost limits!

04:09.130 --> 04:11.280
I will not fail to bring the enemy down!

04:13.800 --> 04:15.520
Scorching heat, gather now.

04:15.520 --> 04:18.570
Cage ablaze, fill now with spirit and will!

04:19.000 --> 04:22.330
<i>The Fiery Heat Blast is a standard spell 
for mid-level magicians.</i>

04:22.900 --> 04:25.400
<i>As tier-three magic, 
it isn't particularly high-level.</i>

04:25.400 --> 04:26.040
<i>However...</i>

04:26.380 --> 04:28.490
<i>since I increased my magical power 
with that secret art,</i>

04:28.490 --> 04:30.620
<i>it will surpass the Seven Thunder Gods.</i>

04:30.620 --> 04:34.670
<i>I'm used to using the Fiery Heat Blast, 
so there is no chance that I will fail.</i>

04:34.910 --> 04:37.580
Prisoner of flames, I release your—

04:41.240 --> 04:43.300
<i>Th-The enemies' memories?</i>

04:47.190 --> 04:48.940
In that case, I'll tell 
you something special.

04:49.610 --> 04:52.860
There is exactly one chance 
to save the witch.

04:54.630 --> 04:57.960
There are ruins in which a mage 
who can control time is said to live...

04:57.960 --> 04:59.900
the great labyrinth.

04:59.900 --> 05:02.880
<i>Th-They're doing this for love and loyalty?</i>

05:02.880 --> 05:04.260
<i>To atone?</i>

05:05.310 --> 05:07.670
<i>If I bring down the evil spirit like this,</i>

05:07.670 --> 05:09.490
<i>there's no way to save 
the ninja and his allies.</i>

05:10.060 --> 05:12.410
<i>But I have...</i>

05:19.400 --> 05:22.060
<i>I have... I...</i>

05:27.900 --> 05:29.140
I'm sorry!

05:37.690 --> 05:40.650
<b>And so time began to pass once more</b>

05:44.170 --> 05:46.140
Blast it!

06:06.560 --> 06:08.650
It's crumbling.

06:15.340 --> 06:17.440
Did you do it, you old geezer?

06:29.570 --> 06:31.500
I took care of it.

06:37.160 --> 06:38.280
Grandpa!

06:38.280 --> 06:39.130
Geezer!

06:39.130 --> 06:40.230
Morlock-san!

06:46.220 --> 06:48.650
Lafa, can you reattach this?

06:48.650 --> 06:50.340
I can, but...

06:50.340 --> 06:53.000
Raelza, can you pick up 
Grandpa's hand for him?

06:53.000 --> 06:55.600
Not that. Mine can wait.

06:56.080 --> 06:57.850
I mean this girl's wings.

06:57.850 --> 06:58.860
What?

06:58.860 --> 07:03.520
Summoning the evil spirit used 
the magic stored in her wings.

07:03.520 --> 07:05.860
The wings themselves 
weren't used up as a catalyst.

07:05.860 --> 07:08.360
Her wings have fallen over there somewhere.

07:08.360 --> 07:09.540
B-But...

07:09.540 --> 07:12.390
They tried to kill us.

07:12.390 --> 07:14.370
We don't have any obligation to help them.

07:16.110 --> 07:20.590
Just before I released my magic, 
I saw their memories.

07:20.590 --> 07:24.380
Once I did, I couldn't kill them anymore.

07:24.870 --> 07:27.900
That's why I used half my magic to attack,

07:27.900 --> 07:30.280
dealing just enough damage 
so as not to kill them,

07:30.280 --> 07:34.180
and at the same time, 
activated Magic Cancellation.

07:34.180 --> 07:36.440
It succeeded wonderfully.

07:37.420 --> 07:39.220
But your arm...

07:39.220 --> 07:43.110
Yes. I had half the magic flow backwards,

07:43.110 --> 07:47.240
so the backlash from the Fiery 
Heat Blast ended up blowing it off.

07:47.710 --> 07:49.160
Geezer...

07:51.960 --> 07:53.580
You stupid old geezer!

07:54.150 --> 07:56.320
Ow! That hurts!

07:56.600 --> 07:58.490
Well, he is her foster father, right?

07:58.490 --> 08:00.040
Right?

08:00.080 --> 08:03.500
<b>Dealing with 
the Enemy</b>

08:03.880 --> 08:07.050
Ninia, my dear, when you use joining magic,

08:07.050 --> 08:10.360
you use your own bodily fluids 
as a catalyst, is that right?

08:10.360 --> 08:11.510
Y-Yes.

08:11.510 --> 08:14.880
I sure would like for you 
to reattach this old man's hand.

08:14.900 --> 08:16.890
What?

08:19.620 --> 08:23.940
If Mister Monpui helps, 
and I use lots of magic,

08:23.940 --> 08:25.780
I can reattach it without using a catalyst.

08:25.780 --> 08:28.740
Ow! You dratted monk! Hold it more gently!

08:30.200 --> 08:31.480
I am holding it.

08:36.310 --> 08:38.200
Lafa! I found her wings.

08:38.200 --> 08:39.900
That's our Saitou!

08:39.900 --> 08:41.670
You're so good at finding things!

08:43.590 --> 08:45.630
I'll act as support for her magic.

08:45.630 --> 08:47.660
Thank you, Guivre-san.

08:48.280 --> 08:50.920
Y-You're quite welcome.

08:51.240 --> 08:52.920
I'll reattach them now.

08:52.920 --> 08:54.220
Don't.

08:54.630 --> 08:56.540
I won't accept charity.

08:56.540 --> 08:59.140
Not from someone who's getting 
along so happily with humans.

09:01.920 --> 09:05.110
Being made an attraction... 
Being sold for money...

09:05.110 --> 09:07.580
You've never experienced that, have you?

09:10.600 --> 09:12.690
But you and the ninja...

09:12.690 --> 09:15.110
a human, are getting along just fine, right?

09:29.840 --> 09:31.350
I have a favor to ask.

09:31.350 --> 09:35.090
Please let those demons go back 
to the demon realm.

09:36.040 --> 09:39.200
They're just always at my stronghold.

09:39.200 --> 09:41.700
It isn't that they've been summoned 
from the demon realm.

09:41.700 --> 09:45.390
Even if I told them to go back, 
they probably wouldn't.

09:45.400 --> 09:49.640
You mean that they're following 
you of their own free will?

09:49.640 --> 09:50.830
Yes.

09:50.830 --> 09:54.910
Up to this point, they've attacked 
a number of parties with me.

09:57.410 --> 10:00.790
The holy knight and magician 
seemed particularly strong,

10:00.790 --> 10:02.820
so to make absolutely sure, 
we ambushed them,

10:02.820 --> 10:05.500
and we thoroughly sliced them up 
so that they couldn't revive.

10:06.500 --> 10:08.320
I'm going to be hanged, right?

10:08.660 --> 10:13.720
But please, let those guys 
and the black fairy go.

10:14.140 --> 10:18.340
Are you looking for the 
mage who can control time?

10:18.660 --> 10:19.700
Yes.

10:19.700 --> 10:22.350
I've heard that the mage's name is Crom.

10:22.350 --> 10:25.800
I think that person is 
the Crom you're looking for.

10:26.870 --> 10:29.270
It's all better! You're very good!

10:29.520 --> 10:32.240
I'd like to make sure 
it's properly reattached.

10:32.240 --> 10:35.060
Ninia, allow me to feel your breasts.

10:35.060 --> 10:36.210
No.

10:37.520 --> 10:40.480
You may feel this humble 
priest's nose instead.

10:41.200 --> 10:42.640
That...

10:42.640 --> 10:45.200
That's Crom, the mage who can control time?

10:45.200 --> 10:50.460
The name of Crom, void rank, 
first class magician, is famous in the east.

10:50.720 --> 10:55.140
For a time, the fact that he had set out for 
this great labyrinth was much talked about.

10:55.140 --> 10:57.420
Though that was over ten years ago.

10:57.420 --> 11:00.380
Ninia, it still hurts.

11:00.380 --> 11:02.380
As I said, you may feel my nose.

11:02.380 --> 11:03.520
Master...

11:03.520 --> 11:06.400
It appeared that your 
memories had returned, but...

11:06.400 --> 11:09.160
Th-That man could...

11:09.810 --> 11:12.320
You're saying that he can save her?

11:17.690 --> 11:19.150
Magically-controlled swords?!

11:21.540 --> 11:24.780
You will leave their punishment to us.

11:25.160 --> 11:27.300
Th-They're...

11:27.300 --> 11:30.170
We have that right, you see.

11:30.170 --> 11:32.320
We will not allow you to call us cowardly!

11:32.320 --> 11:34.660
Feel the shame of being 
caught in a surprise attack!

11:34.660 --> 11:36.040
Don't!

11:37.140 --> 11:38.550
Kisurugi!

11:48.440 --> 11:50.910
Are you all right, boss?

11:51.290 --> 11:52.350
Ableth!

11:52.350 --> 11:55.290
Th-This is nothing.

11:55.290 --> 11:56.900
I'm a demon, after all.

11:56.900 --> 11:58.840
Demo—knight captain.

11:58.840 --> 12:01.410
Indeed. They're of my race?

12:09.700 --> 12:14.210
Don't you lay a hand 
on the boss, you filthy human.

12:14.210 --> 12:15.880
Human?

12:16.280 --> 12:19.680
Who do you take me for...

12:19.680 --> 12:21.140
youngster?

12:22.650 --> 12:24.140
Uncle Dorg?

12:27.840 --> 12:32.480
It can't be... Are you my younger 
brother Tahleg's son, Tahlefon?

12:32.480 --> 12:34.040
That's right!

12:34.040 --> 12:35.990
You can't tell by looking 
at my magnificent horns?

12:35.990 --> 12:39.860
Well, I mean, the last time I saw you 
was several hundred years ago.

12:39.860 --> 12:42.490
And you've gotten a lot burlier since then.

12:42.490 --> 12:43.360
What's going on?

12:43.360 --> 12:44.540
Do you know them?

12:44.540 --> 12:45.750
No, I don't.

12:45.750 --> 12:48.700
But that holy knight is definitely a demon.

12:48.700 --> 12:50.760
And a pretty highly ranked one, at that.

12:50.760 --> 12:52.340
Hey, Uncle.

12:52.340 --> 12:56.050
Didn't you say you were gonna 
conquer the human lands one day?

12:56.050 --> 12:57.540
Well, you see,

12:57.540 --> 12:59.900
I ended up getting beaten 
by the king of a certain kingdom.

12:59.900 --> 13:01.310
That's so pathetic!

13:01.310 --> 13:03.190
And what are you doing, huh?

13:03.190 --> 13:05.230
Well, I was beaten, too, by the boss...

13:05.230 --> 13:08.070
that ninja, so I became 
his sworn younger brother.

13:08.080 --> 13:09.020
Huh?

13:09.020 --> 13:10.540
Hang on, Uncle...

13:10.540 --> 13:12.980
That means you lost twice, 
once to the king and once to the boss!

13:12.980 --> 13:14.340
You lost to humans!

13:14.340 --> 13:16.690
Shut up! I let down my guard, that's all!

13:16.940 --> 13:20.630
Well, when it comes to underhanded 
methods like sneak attacks,

13:20.630 --> 13:23.580
the boss is worse than a demon, 
so I guess you couldn't help it.

13:24.960 --> 13:28.900
Say, how many people have
 their sneak attacks <i>actually</i> killed?

13:28.900 --> 13:30.770
Um, if I remember rightly...

13:30.770 --> 13:33.380
there are two who haven't 
been confirmed as revived.

13:33.380 --> 13:37.420
I heard that they're a holy knight 
and magician from a neighboring kingdom.

13:37.420 --> 13:39.380
Could those two be...

13:39.380 --> 13:41.510
Regarding the fact that you 
were beaten twice by humans...

13:41.510 --> 13:43.560
I'm going to relay that to the king.

13:43.560 --> 13:45.340
Minister, that would be...

13:45.740 --> 13:48.340
They're alive now, right? Which means...

13:48.340 --> 13:53.230
If those two were to forgive him, 
then he could avoid getting hanged, right?

13:53.670 --> 13:56.680
Saitou, you're all right with that? 
They nearly killed you!

13:57.410 --> 13:58.680
I...

13:59.400 --> 14:01.030
<i>The magic light can be on the dim side.</i>

14:01.030 --> 14:02.650
<i>This guy is a weakling!</i>

14:02.650 --> 14:03.660
Saitou!

14:04.410 --> 14:06.370
It doesn't bother me.

14:06.370 --> 14:09.740
And we heard about the circumstances 
they're facing from Morlock-san.

14:16.860 --> 14:19.850
So, to return that witch to normal,

14:19.850 --> 14:24.500
you came to the great labyrinth in search 
of the mage who can control time?

14:24.500 --> 14:25.340
Yes.

14:25.690 --> 14:27.260
Are you Crom?

14:27.260 --> 14:28.510
If you are, then...

14:28.710 --> 14:32.790
I'm sorry, but there isn't any magic 
that can reverse just one section of time.

14:32.790 --> 14:37.520
What I can use is magic which 
temporarily stops time, and...

14:39.230 --> 14:40.940
No, that's about it.

14:40.940 --> 14:42.080
<i>Master...</i>

14:42.080 --> 14:44.240
<i>Have your memories returned after all?</i>

14:44.240 --> 14:45.740
It can't be.

14:45.980 --> 14:50.680
If there were anyone who could 
do it, it would be that guy.

14:50.680 --> 14:51.740
That guy?

14:51.740 --> 14:54.810
The one who tested time 
and space magic here,

14:54.810 --> 14:58.240
a mage more advanced and mysterious than I.

14:59.120 --> 15:05.000
The one who summoned the items from 
another dimension was probably him, too.

15:05.000 --> 15:07.760
Then, boss, if we find him...

15:07.760 --> 15:08.860
Won't work.

15:09.540 --> 15:13.760
He grew tired of this world 
and went somewhere else.

15:14.000 --> 15:15.480
You're impressive.

15:15.480 --> 15:18.450
I've already grown tired of this world,

15:18.450 --> 15:21.650
but I'm glad that I was able to 
fight someone like you here at the end.

15:21.650 --> 15:24.100
W-Wait...

15:24.820 --> 15:27.490
I'm journeying to another world.

15:28.600 --> 15:31.760
I have no idea where he might have gone.

15:31.760 --> 15:35.120
The Demon Realm, 
the Spirit Realm, or perhaps...

15:35.120 --> 15:38.880
The world I came from... Is that possible?

15:38.890 --> 15:42.130
Yes. Finding him would be impossible.

15:45.620 --> 15:48.550
That witch... There's a way to save her.

15:50.400 --> 15:53.440
Uncle's ally... the magician?

15:53.440 --> 15:55.440
I-Is that true?

15:55.740 --> 15:57.040
Very likely.

15:57.430 --> 15:59.340
Judging from your magical energy,

15:59.340 --> 16:02.180
you seem to be a first-class magician.

16:02.180 --> 16:04.940
Are you saying you can 
use rejuvenation magic?

16:04.940 --> 16:07.780
Yes, though it's actually my ki—

16:08.440 --> 16:10.590
my friend, a magic knight who can use it.

16:12.070 --> 16:15.070
That man is capable 
of doing something like that?

16:15.070 --> 16:17.440
Does magic like that truly exist?

16:17.440 --> 16:20.830
I've heard that only gods can use it.

16:20.830 --> 16:25.160
That means, if they cast that for us, 
then the lady witch can be saved?

16:25.160 --> 16:27.840
That's great! Boss, we did it!

16:27.840 --> 16:29.840
Y-Yes.

16:30.590 --> 16:35.340
However, that magic 
requires something specific.

16:36.020 --> 16:37.370
That is...

16:39.250 --> 16:43.220
the life of someone connected 
to the one to be rejuvenated.

16:46.900 --> 16:48.750
B-Boss, you can't!

16:48.750 --> 16:50.160
It's out of the question!

16:50.160 --> 16:52.640
There has to be some other way! Right?

16:52.640 --> 16:54.820
Boss! You can't do it! 
Let's find another way! All right?

16:54.820 --> 16:55.980
Boss!

17:00.590 --> 17:03.120
Please use my life.

17:03.520 --> 17:05.000
Boss!

17:05.000 --> 17:07.520
Kisurugi! I'll do it!

17:08.570 --> 17:11.230
Primasse, don't say it if you can't do it.

17:11.230 --> 17:15.050
And we don't know if such a 
little life as yours will be effective.

17:15.050 --> 17:16.800
B-But...

17:17.470 --> 17:19.520
If I'm to be hanged anyway,

17:19.520 --> 17:22.310
I'd rather use this life 
for the woman I love.

17:27.990 --> 17:30.270
I know it's a selfish request...

17:31.830 --> 17:32.880
but I beg of you.

17:34.840 --> 17:38.820
Rightly, this is where you 
should be torn limb from limb...

17:38.820 --> 17:41.540
but you are a friend to my nephew Tahlefon.

17:41.860 --> 17:43.680
Minister, may I ask this of you?

17:43.680 --> 17:44.520
Uncle!

17:44.520 --> 17:45.530
We said no!

17:45.840 --> 17:47.580
Tahlefon, Ableth.

17:47.580 --> 17:50.540
This is the only way. 
You know that, don't you?

17:51.100 --> 17:52.980
B-Boss...

17:54.960 --> 17:59.080
The criminal must be dealt with in 
accordance with this kingdom's laws...

17:59.080 --> 18:00.970
is what I'd like to say.

18:00.970 --> 18:05.080
But if everyone here would 
pretend they never saw his crimes,

18:05.080 --> 18:06.730
then we may do as we like.

18:06.730 --> 18:10.980
I think that if his life can be 
used to save another's...

18:10.980 --> 18:14.110
then that's one way 
of atoning for his crimes.

18:14.110 --> 18:16.610
This is too complicated. 
Just do as you like.

18:16.900 --> 18:19.340
We won't tell anyone.

18:19.340 --> 18:21.850
Sacrificing yourself for love... 
I understand that.

18:21.850 --> 18:23.550
I'm against it!

18:23.550 --> 18:25.800
As the kingdom's officially 
recognized hero—

18:25.800 --> 18:29.360
As his instructor, I will teach him 
how to walk a moral path.

18:29.360 --> 18:30.410
Don't worry.

18:30.700 --> 18:32.630
I really don't care.

18:32.630 --> 18:34.760
I oppose this as well.

18:34.760 --> 18:36.380
If there is not mutual consent,

18:36.380 --> 18:38.460
adventurers who fight 
within the great labyrinth

18:38.460 --> 18:40.380
must be reported to the authorities.

18:40.760 --> 18:42.130
However...

18:42.760 --> 18:44.500
Magician.

18:44.500 --> 18:48.600
You have some connection to 
King Maderaka of this kingdom, don't you?

18:48.600 --> 18:50.900
I believe this matter 
can be entrusted to you.

18:50.900 --> 18:52.740
He figured out that you're the minister.

18:52.740 --> 18:53.890
Yes.

18:53.890 --> 18:56.230
He nearly killed me, but...

18:56.240 --> 18:58.400
Let him decide how he wants to die.

18:58.400 --> 19:02.240
I saw the reason you did 
battle in your memories.

19:02.240 --> 19:04.400
You should accomplish your dearest desire.

19:04.690 --> 19:06.140
It's all right, isn't it?

19:07.040 --> 19:08.410
Kisurugi...

19:08.790 --> 19:11.400
I'm in favor. What about you, Saitou?

19:12.520 --> 19:13.810
I...

19:27.890 --> 19:31.670
He wanted to be of use to someone...

19:31.670 --> 19:34.940
and if this is the only way 
that wish can come true...

19:36.380 --> 19:38.520
I hope that he'll be allowed to do so.

19:39.490 --> 19:42.910
<b>The Handyman 
and the Assassin</b>

19:44.950 --> 19:46.640
We open a new window,

19:46.640 --> 19:49.870
and the names of those we 
send home through it are...

19:47.400 --> 19:49.390
This isn't right, little fairy!

19:49.390 --> 19:50.400
Boss!

19:49.870 --> 19:51.460
the Young Noble of the Furious Horns,

19:50.400 --> 19:52.340
Is this all we meant to you?

19:51.460 --> 19:53.520
Tahlefon Defotogrogel III,

19:52.340 --> 19:55.290
The spell for sending them 
to the demon realm is difficult,

19:53.520 --> 19:54.630
and his friend,

19:54.630 --> 20:01.380
the Wings of the Black 
Malediction, Ableth Zalnetgatus.

19:55.290 --> 19:58.420
but if you know their lineage 
and their true names,

19:58.420 --> 20:00.350
the degree of difficulty drops considerably.

20:00.350 --> 20:01.880
And for the magical energy she lacks,

20:01.880 --> 20:03.800
she can just have Grandpa 
share some with her.

20:03.800 --> 20:05.810
I'm not going back!

20:06.610 --> 20:07.770
Blast you!

20:18.230 --> 20:20.690
Have the demons returned home?

20:21.020 --> 20:22.000
Yes.

20:22.480 --> 20:27.410
I contacted the king— 
the person who can break the curse.

20:27.410 --> 20:30.330
I will use teleportation magic 
to take you to him now.

20:38.020 --> 20:38.920
Well, then.

20:47.320 --> 20:48.440
Wait, please.

20:48.440 --> 20:50.430
There is just one thing bothering me.

20:52.260 --> 20:53.350
You...

20:53.350 --> 20:55.930
Those clothes. Where are they from?

20:55.930 --> 20:56.950
What?

20:57.680 --> 21:01.390
Pardon me, but you seem 
to be the weakest one here.

21:01.390 --> 21:04.070
And yet, you moved as though you 
were at the heart of the team.

21:04.440 --> 21:06.070
That's something that I could see.

21:06.370 --> 21:09.820
If you hadn't been here, 
then we might have won.

21:11.200 --> 21:13.710
Are you a ninja from a country I don't know of?

21:13.710 --> 21:15.710
What? No.

21:16.450 --> 21:18.960
I'm just a handyman.

21:20.180 --> 21:21.670
A handyman.

21:25.940 --> 21:27.460
I see.

21:33.090 --> 21:34.480
Well, then.

21:36.480 --> 21:39.980
<b>And so the assassin, who had been needed in the world of darkness...</b>

21:51.490 --> 21:57.500
<b>stood before the handyman, who had tried very hard to be needed in another world...</b>

22:03.000 --> 22:10.010
<b>and vanished</b>

22:30.320 --> 22:33.120
<i>Like being gently carried away on a current</i>

22:33.120 --> 22:35.780
<i>Like drifting off to sleep at night</i>

22:35.780 --> 22:38.030
<i>Like there's nothing 
particularly special about it</i>

22:38.030 --> 22:40.010
<i>Our hearts are one</i>

22:40.010 --> 22:42.850
<i>“See you later” illuminates the way</i>

22:42.850 --> 22:44.860
<i>To the depths of the future</i>

22:44.860 --> 22:49.740
<i>Where kindness is the one 
thing I'm certain I felt</i>

22:49.740 --> 22:54.720
<i>You know, I'm sure we 
don't know anything</i>

22:54.720 --> 22:59.670
<i>But you know, for right now, that’s fine</i>

22:59.670 --> 23:02.350
<i>I'm waiting, I'm waiting</i>

23:02.350 --> 23:04.510
<i>Let's sing here again</i>

23:04.510 --> 23:07.300
<i>One day, we'll shine the light</i>

23:07.300 --> 23:09.980
<i>Now, I think I can embrace even my tears</i>

23:09.980 --> 23:12.090
<i>As we picture it, as we paint it</i>

23:12.090 --> 23:14.230
<i>A single bit of warmth is all there is</i>

23:14.230 --> 23:20.790
<i>And now, so that we can 
laugh, let's hold hands</i>

23:20.790 --> 23:26.650
<i>That’s right, it will 
blossom in the skies</i>

23:26.650 --> 23:32.800
<i>A guidepost showing us the way to live</i>
